; Tutorial markdown lives in per-topic subdirectories. The mdx stanza only
; tests files in its own directory, so a (subdir ...) is needed for each.
;
; The tested set is listed explicitly, per subdirectory. It is the set of
; tutorials that currently pass mdx. The remaining tutorials need an editorial
; pass before they can be tested (compiler-version-specific output, code blocks
; authored in a non-mdx-compatible style, cross-block state, blocks that write
; files or run external tools) and are tracked as a follow-up rather than
; silently skipped block by block. The platform/ subdirectory has no tutorial
; with testable OCaml blocks yet, so it has no stanza.
;
; A file in the tested set must verify something: tool/check-mdx-coverage.sh
; fails the build if a listed file has no ocaml/sh/bash block left that mdx
; actually runs (every block `$MDX skip`ped), or uses a fence label mdx
; silently ignores. Without it a file can be "tested" and check nothing.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  %{project_root}/tool/check-mdx-coverage.sh
  dune
  ../exercises/dune
  (glob_files_rec *.md)
  (glob_files ../exercises/*.md))
 (action
  (run sh %{project_root}/tool/check-mdx-coverage.sh dune ../exercises/dune)))

